---
import Gallery from '../../layouts/Gallery.astro';
import Related from '../../components/Related.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Gallery title="Pattern: role home">
  <p class="demo-note">
    <strong>Who uses it</strong>: every named role — a buyer, an approver,
    a warehouse supervisor — each seeing their own version.
    <strong>How often</strong>: the first screen after sign-in, and the one
    they come back to between tasks. <strong>What "done" looks like</strong>:
    the reader knows in one glance whether anything needs them, and leaves
    for the screen that resolves it.
    <strong>Not a launcher</strong> — a tile grid of every app someone
    <em>could</em> open is <a href={base + '/patterns/app-launch'}>app
    launch</a>; this shows live content about <em>their</em> work. And
    <strong>not a dashboard</strong>: the
    <a href={base + '/patterns/reporting-dashboard'}>reporting dashboard</a>
    monitors the <em>business</em> (is the period on track), a role home
    monitors <em>my work</em> (is anything waiting on me). Same widgets,
    different subject — and confusing the two is how a home screen turns
    into a chart wall nobody acts on.
  </p>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>The screen — one role's morning</h2>
    <p class="bo-byline bo-byline--compact">Signed in as J. Kim · Buyer, Rotterdam</p>
    <div class="bo-widget-grid" style="--bo-widget-min: 16rem">
      <section class="bo-widget bo-widget--span-2">
        <div class="bo-widget__header">
          <span class="bo-widget__title">Needs you</span>
          <a class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--secondary" href={base + '/patterns/inbox'}>Open inbox</a>
        </div>
        <div class="bo-widget__body">
          <div class="bo-cluster" style="gap: var(--bo-space-6)">
            <span class="bo-stat">
              <span class="bo-stat__label">Awaiting your approval</span>
              <span class="bo-stat__value">3</span>
              <span class="bo-stat__delta bo-stat__delta--bad"><span aria-hidden="true">▲</span> 1 over 2 days<span class="bo-visually-hidden">, needs attention</span></span>
            </span>
            <span class="bo-stat">
              <span class="bo-stat__label">Exceptions assigned</span>
              <span class="bo-stat__value">2</span>
              <span class="bo-stat__delta bo-stat__delta--bad"><span aria-hidden="true">▲</span> oldest 26 days<span class="bo-visually-hidden">, needs attention</span></span>
            </span>
            <span class="bo-stat">
              <span class="bo-stat__label">Tasks</span>
              <span class="bo-stat__value">1</span>
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="bo-widget">
        <div class="bo-widget__header"><span class="bo-widget__title">My open orders</span></div>
        <div class="bo-widget__body">
          <span class="bo-stat">
            <span class="bo-stat__label">Value in flight</span>
            <span class="bo-stat__value">$184,320</span>
            <span class="bo-stat__delta">across 14 POs</span>
          </span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="bo-widget">
        <div class="bo-widget__header"><span class="bo-widget__title">Period close</span></div>
        <div class="bo-widget__body">
          <p style="margin-block: 0 var(--bo-space-2)">Period 2026-07 · 82% complete</p>
          <progress class="bo-progress" value="82" max="100" aria-label="Period 2026-07 close progress"></progress>
          <p class="bo-u-text-muted" style="margin-block-end: 0">2 of your 11 close tasks remain</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="bo-widget">
        <div class="bo-widget__header">
          <span class="bo-widget__title">Recent</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bo-widget__body">
          <ul class="bo-stack bo-stack--tight docs-list-bare" style="margin: 0">
            <li><a href={base + '/patterns/object-page'}>PO-88213 · Acme Supply Co.</a> <span class="bo-badge bo-badge--warning">Pending approval</span></li>
            <li><a href={base + '/patterns/object-page'}>PO-88219 · Globex Industrial</a> <span class="bo-badge bo-badge--success">Approved</span></li>
            <li><a href={base + '/patterns/list-report'}>Open items · CC-4021</a> <span class="bo-badge">report</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Every number on this screen is <em>about the
    reader</em> — "awaiting <strong>your</strong> approval", "<strong>your</strong>
    11 close tasks" — and every one of them is a link out. A role home that
    cannot be left is a wall; the measure of this screen is how fast people
    leave it for the screen that does the work.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>One pattern, many roles</h2>
    <p>The same markup serves every role — only the card contents change,
    which is why this is one pattern and not one screen per job title. An
    approver's morning above; a warehouse supervisor's below:</p>
    <div class="bo-widget-grid" style="--bo-widget-min: 16rem">
      <section class="bo-widget bo-widget--span-2">
        <div class="bo-widget__header">
          <span class="bo-widget__title">Needs you</span>
          <a class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--secondary" href={base + '/patterns/inbox'}>Open inbox</a>
        </div>
        <div class="bo-widget__body">
          <div class="bo-cluster" style="gap: var(--bo-space-6)">
            <span class="bo-stat">
              <span class="bo-stat__label">Receipts to post</span>
              <span class="bo-stat__value">7</span>
            </span>
            <span class="bo-stat">
              <span class="bo-stat__label">Short deliveries</span>
              <span class="bo-stat__value">2</span>
              <span class="bo-stat__delta bo-stat__delta--bad"><span aria-hidden="true">▲</span> needs decision<span class="bo-visually-hidden">, worse</span></span>
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="bo-widget">
        <div class="bo-widget__header"><span class="bo-widget__title">Dock status</span></div>
        <div class="bo-widget__body">
          <span class="bo-stat">
            <span class="bo-stat__label">Trucks waiting</span>
            <span class="bo-stat__value">3</span>
            <span class="bo-stat__delta">next slot 11:20</span>
          </span>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Identical classes, identical grid, different
    content. Roles differ in <em>what the server sends</em>, never in the
    markup — a per-role screen fork is the thing this pattern exists to
    prevent.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Markup</h2>
    <pre><code>{`<div class="bo-widget-grid" style="--bo-widget-min: 16rem">
  <!-- The one card that must exist: what needs the reader, linking
       into the inbox that holds the rows. -->
  <section class="bo-widget bo-widget--span-2">
    <div class="bo-widget__header">
      <span class="bo-widget__title">Needs you</span>
      <a class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--secondary" href="/inbox">Open inbox</a>
    </div>
    <div class="bo-widget__body">
      <span class="bo-stat">
        <span class="bo-stat__label">Awaiting your approval</span>
        <span class="bo-stat__value">3</span>
        <span class="bo-stat__delta bo-stat__delta--bad">1 over 2 days</span>
      </span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Progress card: the close, a run, an onboarding checklist. -->
  <section class="bo-widget">
    <div class="bo-widget__header"><span class="bo-widget__title">Period close</span></div>
    <div class="bo-widget__body">
      <!-- Native <progress>: value/max semantics and the progressbar
           role come from the platform. Always pair with visible text. -->
      <progress class="bo-progress" value="82" max="100"
                aria-label="Period 2026-07 close progress"></progress>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>`}</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Anatomy</h2>
    <ol class="bo-stack bo-stack--tight docs-list">
      <li><strong>Identity line</strong> — a
      <a href={base + '/components/byline'}>byline</a> naming who is signed
      in and in what role. On a screen whose whole content is "yours", the
      reader must be able to see whose.</li>
      <li><strong>"Needs you" card</strong> — the one card that must exist,
      spanning two columns, counting what the
      <a href={base + '/patterns/inbox'}>inbox</a> holds and linking
      straight into it. This card is a summary OF the inbox, never a second
      copy of its logic. This is the human-monitoring signal — the
      AI-manages/human-monitors split below names it explicitly.</li>
      <li><strong>Stat cards</strong> —
      <a href={base + '/components/dashboard'}>stats</a> with a label,
      value, and a delta that carries its meaning in words plus a glyph
      (two-channel: "1 over 2 days" is the text, the tone is the echo).</li>
      <li><strong>Progress card</strong> — a
      <a href={base + '/components/progress'}>progress bar</a> for anything
      with a finish line: the period close, a posting run, onboarding.</li>
      <li><strong>Recent</strong> — links back to what the reader touched;
      the cheapest useful card in the set.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Data contract</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Request</th><th scope="col">Returns / on failure</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">GET /home</td><td>the grid shell with each card as its own fragment slot — the page must render before the slowest card resolves</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">GET /home/cards/:name</td><td>one card, loaded independently (<code>hx-trigger="load"</code>); one slow query must never hold the whole screen — the reporting dashboard's contract, same reason</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">counts</td><td>every "needs you" number comes from the SAME query the inbox uses, not a parallel one — two sources for one number is how a home screen starts lying</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">per-role content</td><td>the server decides which cards a role gets; the client never hides cards it received, because a hidden card is still a leaked fact</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted"><strong>The AI-manages / human-monitors
    split, stated</strong>: this screen is almost entirely the human's
    side — it is the oversight surface for work agents are doing
    underneath. Its one machine-facing rule is the counts contract above:
    an agent that resolves an inbox row must move this screen's number
    with it, because a stale "3 awaiting" is worse than no number at all.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>States</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">State</th><th scope="col">What ships</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Nothing needs you</td><td>the "needs you" card says so as a <strong>success</strong> — "Nothing is waiting on you" — matching the inbox's own empty state; the card stays, it never disappears (a missing card reads as a broken card)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Card still loading</td><td>a <a href={base + '/components/state-patterns'}>skeleton</a> inside that card only; the rest of the screen is already usable</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Card failed</td><td>that card shows the failure and a retry, and the others carry on — one dead query must not blank the home screen</td></tr>
          <tr><td>New role / first day</td><td>cards render with real zeros and an explanation, never an empty grid: "No orders yet — your first PO will appear here"</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Permission-limited role</td><td>the server simply does not send those cards; nothing on screen hints at what was withheld</td></tr>
          <tr><td>No JS</td><td>fully functional — this page has no JS dependency; every card is static markup and there is no <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> block to lose</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Components used</h2>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted"><span class="bo-badge">complexity 2 of 4</span></p>
    <ul class="bo-cluster docs-list-bare">
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/dashboard'}>Dashboard</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/progress'}>Progress</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/badge'}>Badge</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/byline'}>Byline</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/button'}>Button</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <Related links={[
    ["/patterns/inbox", "Inbox"],
    ["/patterns/app-launch", "App launch"],
    ["/patterns/reporting-dashboard", "Reporting dashboard"],
    ["/components/dashboard", "Dashboard & widgets"],
  ]} />
</Gallery>
